              "text": "{\n  \"query_text\": \"According to WHO guidelines, what are the specific recommended intake limits for free sugars to manage body weight throughout the lifecourse, and why is using non-sugar sweeteners (NSS) conditionally recommended against as a method to achieve this weight control?\",\n  \"target_population\": [\n    \"adults\",\n    \"children\"\n  ],\n  \"conditions\": [\n    \"weight control\",\n    \"reducing free sugars intake\"\n  ],\n  \"draft_rationale\": \"To answer this query, the user must combine information from both passages. The 2015 guideline provides the specific intake limits for free sugars (reducing to less than 10% of total energy intake, and conditionally below 5%) to manage body weight throughout the lifecourse. The 2023 guideline provides the conditional recommendation against using non-sugar sweeteners (NSS) for weight control, explaining that there is no evidence of long-term benefit on body fatness in adults or children, alongside potential long-term risks like type 2 diabetes, CVDs, and mortality in adults.\"\n}",
